  "description": "Dinic flow. addsol returns state; add returns pair<state,state>. state supports from/to, equality by owner and indices, and get/add/set_flow/cap in O(1). Nonconst it_idx(vertex,f)/it_all(f) call f(state) for original edges, including zero-capacity edges, in vertex/adjacency insertion order; callbacks may modify flow/capacity but must not insert edges or clear the graph during traversal. States survive insertion/reset/build and require their original owner alive, uncleared and unmoved. Mutations must preserve valid capacities and flow conservation. build(st,en,limit=INF) resets and computes flow, returning void; ret() reads its stored result in O(1), valid after build until input changes. min_cut(st) returns a residual reachable vector<bool> in O(n+m), representing a minimum cut when the sink is unreachable after exhausting flow; reachable(st,en) reuses it. get_edge/get_rev return read-only references that insertion or clear may invalidate."
